{"archetypes":[{"name":"scope-guard","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan may expand beyond the approved issue scope by adding Step 0 parent rehydration despite the scope anchor limiting SKILL.md work to the Step 5 banner area.","prompt_body":"Compare the staged description’s approved direction and scope files against the plan’s proposed edits, looking for additions that exceed the issue’s three intended DX/doc-hardening fixes. Pay special attention to whether Step 0 parent-shell rehydration is justified by repo evidence or is a larger behavioral/documentation change than the scope permits. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-state","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The fixes depend on subtle shell boundaries: exported child env, parent Bash fence state, sourced library inertness, and same-subprocess banner variables.","prompt_body":"Audit the plan’s shell-state assumptions against the actual script and SKILL fences, especially child-process exports from implement-bootstrap-invoke.sh versus variables needed later in the parent Step 0 shell. Check that the proposed direct-exec CLI for lib-implement-round-cap.sh cannot disturb sourced behavior and that Step 5 banner values are computed in the same subprocess that prints them and launches the review loop. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"harness-wiring","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan adds and extends tests, Makefile targets, sibling docs, and lint exclusions where wiring omissions could leave the proposed contracts unverified.","prompt_body":"Review whether each planned script contract change has the right offline harness coverage, Makefile registration, shard inclusion, sibling markdown, and agent-lint treatment for this repository’s conventions. Look for mismatches between the stated acceptance criteria and the actual proposed test commands, especially around append-execution-issue.sh usage output and lib-implement-round-cap.sh direct execution. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
